 "notes": "Each item is one (corpus slice, harness identity split) pair measured by scripts/hillclimb/benches/speaker_autoeval.py through `speaker-eval-harness autoeval`. `corpus` must equal the `corpus` field of a FingerprintCache in the manifest (or a family like `ami`, which sums every ami_* slice). Splits are pinned, never hashed: harness `train` and `dev` identities feed the climber's dev split, harness `holdout` identities feed the climber's holdout. The harness splits people by FNV-1a(family|speaker), so every audio-quality variant of one person stays on one side and dev/holdout never share a person. holdout_fraction is unused because every item pins its split. Items inside one family share people (the same speakers in different audio qualities), so they are correlated; paired-bootstrap CIs across items are optimistic. The holdout confirmation is the honest check. Input needed on the Mac (gitignored, ~11 GB): data/eval/qmatrix/<corpus>_<quality>/fingerprints.json FingerprintCache files ({corpus, meetings:[{meeting, order, speakers:[{gtSpeaker, embedding[256], durationSeconds, segmentCount, clusterCount, purity}]}]}, AutoResearchModels.swift) plus a manifest made with `cd data/eval/qmatrix && shasum -a 256 */fingerprints.json > ../qmatrix-manifest.sha256`. Nothing in this repo produces these caches: docs cite an out-of-tree `ladder-fingerprints` harness command that main.swift does not have. Copy them onto the Mac from wherever they were built. The quality list mirrors SpeakerExemplarDeltaEvalTests.swift (ami: 6 qualities, voxceleb: 10). If the local manifest holds different caches, the missing ones come back as item errors naming the slices the report does have; edit the items (or point items_file at a local list) to match. VoxConverse and ICSI have no fingerprint caches anywhere yet, so they have no items.",
